.TH ZSHRC 1 "2026-09-04" "hoolies" "User Commands"
.SH NAME
zshrc \- interactive zsh configuration
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B ?
.RI [ OPTION ]...
.SH DESCRIPTION
This is the help for the interactive
.B ~/.zshrc
(a symlink to this directory's
.BR .zshrc ).
Type
.B ?
and Enter to read this page.
.SH OPTIONS
Mandatory arguments to long options are mandatory for short options too.
.TP
.BR \-h ", " \-\-help
display a short usage summary and exit
.SH COMMANDS
.TP
.B ?
display this manual
.TP
.B y
open yazi and
.B cd
to the directory you leave in
.TP
.B showpath
print
.B PATH
one directory per line (green if it exists, red if not)
.TP
.B up
.RI [ N ]
.B cd
up one directory, or
.I N
directories
.TP
.B cl
.RI [ DIR ]
.B cd
to
.I DIR
(or
.B HOME
if omitted), then
.B ls \-la .
.I DIR
may be a path,
.BR \- ,
.BR +N " / " \-N
(same as
.BR cd ),
a
.B dirs \-v
index, or
.BR ~N .
.TP
.B fe
pick files with
.B fd
and
.B fzf
(bat preview) and open them in
.B $EDITOR
.TP
.B bak
.I FILE
copy
.I FILE
to
.IB FILE .YYYYMMDD-HHMMSS
.TP
.B _hoolies_update_zsh_plugins
fast-forward every git plugin under
.B ~/.zsh
.SH ALIASES
.TP
.B d
.B dirs \-v
(directory stack)
.TP
.B ls
.B ls \-\-color=auto \-A \-\-group\-directories\-first
.TP
.B ll
long listing, hidden files, newest last
.TP
.B l.
list only hidden names in the current directory
.TP
.BR dmesg ", " diff ", " grep ", " ip
color output (dmesg is piped to
.BR less )
.SH KEY BINDINGS
Emacs layout
.RB ( bindkey\ \-e ).
.TP
.BR Home " / " End " / " Delete
beginning of line, end of line, delete character
.TP
.B Shift-Tab
move backward in the completion menu
.TP
.B Ctrl-X Ctrl-E
edit the current command in
.B $EDITOR
.TP
.B Ctrl-Space
accept the autosuggestion
.TP
.BR Up " / " Down " / " Ctrl-P " / " Ctrl-N
search history for the current prefix
.TP
.B Ctrl-T
fzf file insert (bat preview)
.TP
.B Alt-C
fzf directory
.B cd
(tree preview)
.TP
.B Ctrl-R
fzf history with timestamps; inserts the command only
.TP
.B Tab
RTFM / completion (not fzf completion)
.TP
.BR Ctrl-W " / " Alt-B " / " Alt-F
stop at slashes, not whole paths
.SH PROMPT
Two lines: cwd in cyan, then the last exit status.
After a command, its wall-clock duration is right-aligned in yellow
on the path line
.RI ( 0.42s ,
.IR 1m05s ,
.IR 1h02m03s ).
Pressing Enter with an empty line hides the duration.
A blank line is inserted after command output.
On tall terminals a spacer keeps the prompt off the bottom edge.
The terminal title is the running command, or
.B ~/...
at the prompt.
.SH DIRECTORY STACK
.BR AUTO_PUSHD
and
.B PUSHD_IGNORE_DUPS
are on.
.B cd ,
.B up ,
and
.B cl
push the previous directory without printing the stack.
.B DIRSTACKSIZE
is 16.
Use
.BR d ,
.BR "cd \-" ,
.BR "cl \-" ,
.BR ~1 ,
.BR ~2 ,
.BR "cl 1" .
.B AUTO_CD
is off.
.SH PATH
User bins are prepended, missing directories are dropped,
duplicates are removed:
.BR /usr/local/go/bin ,
.BR ~/.cargo/bin ,
.BR ~/go/bin ,
.BR ~/.local/bin ,
then the inherited
.BR PATH .
.B EDITOR
and
.B VISUAL
are
.BR vim .
.SH HISTORY
File:
.BR ~/.local/state/zsh/history
(or
.B $XDG_STATE_HOME/zsh/history ).
10 000 lines, shared, extended timestamps.
Duplicates and leading-space lines are not saved.
Unknown command names (typos) are not saved.
.B HIST_VERIFY
expands history before running it.
.SH COMPLETION
Menu select, case-insensitive matching, cached under
.BR ~/.cache/zsh/zcompcache .
.B ls
colors are applied to completion lists when
.B dircolors
exists.
.SH PLUGINS
Installed on demand into
.BR ~/.zsh :
fzf-dir-navigator, zsh-autosuggestions, zsh-history-substring-search,
zsh-rtfm, zsh-syntax-highlighting.
URL quoting and bracketed paste are enabled.
Syntax highlighting is loaded last.
.SH FILES
.TP
.B ~/.zshrc
symlink to the tracked
.B .zshrc
.TP
.B zshrc.1
this manual, in the same directory as the tracked
.B .zshrc
.TP
.B ~/.local/state/zsh/history
command history
.TP
.B ~/.zsh
plugins
.SH SEE ALSO
.BR zsh (1),
.BR zshzle (1),
.BR fzf (1),
.BR fd (1),
.BR yazi (1)
